      "title": "Valdosta State University Careers",
      "description": "Careers Skip to Main Content Press Control+M to start dragging object ptnbsid=VlfGyxmDOX0IbneDOLY13ml9K2c%3d Back Valdosta State University Careers Search Category Name Search keywords Search in... Menu Category All Company Directory Job Data No results to display Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Title Actions Search My Preferences Help Sign Out Valdosta State University Careers More Actions Welcome Sign In New User Thank you for your interest in employment at Valdosta State University. You can search and review job openings from this page without creating an account with us. When you are ready to apply, login or create a new applicant account. You can access this applicant portal on your desktop, laptop, or any mobile device, and you will be able to: View all job opportunities Search on specific criteria to find jobs that interest you Set up a search agent that will notify you when positions are posted that match your search criteria For technical support or assistance completing a job application, please contact the USG Service Desk at (877) 251-2644 or support@usg.edu . For questions about positions at Valdosta State University, please contact the Office of Human Resources at (229) 333-5709. Due to an Oracle Known Issue, Mac OS users are advised to browse and apply for jobs using a web browser other than Safari. The Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act and the Higher Education Act (HEA) fire safety provisions require institutions of higher education to publish an Annual Security Report and Annual Fire Safety Report. These reports include crime and fire statistics for the three most recently completed calendar years, institutional policies and procedures for reporting crimes, and current policies concerning the security of, and access to, campus facilities and residences, as well as security considerations in the maintenance of campus facilities. The reports are available online at: https://www.valdosta.edu/administration/finance-admin/police/clery-act.php . If you would like to retain a copy of the report, you may print it from your browser or request a paper copy by emailing the institution at openrecords@valdosta.edu .. View All Jobs My Job Notifications My Job Applications My Favorite Jobs My Saved Searches My Account Information Valdosta State University Careers Sign In New User"
    },
    "https://www.valdosta.edu/administration/finance-admin/human-resources/documents/marsha-simon-perm-notice-of-faculty-position.pdf": {
      "title": "NOTICE OF FACULTY POSITION",
      "description": "NOTICE OF FACULTY POSITION \n \nAssistant Professor (Research) \n \nResponsibilities: Teaching and research in the area of educational research design and methods, as well \nas service to the department, college, and university. The selected candidate will be responsible for \nteaching courses in the candidate’s area of expertise, creating and publishing scholarly works, and \nproviding service to the department, college, and university. Required Qualifications: Doctorate in \nResearch Methods, Evaluation & Measurement, Educational Statistics, or a related educational field.  If \nqualified for this position, or if you can refer a qualified candidate, please contact Steve Downey, Ph.D., \nChair of the Department of Leadership, Technology, and Workforce Development, Valdosta State \nUniversity. \n \nDate posted:_09/04/2024 \n \nLocation of Posting: \nhttps://www.valdosta.edu/administration/finance-admin/human-resources/employment-\nopportunities.php \n \n \nDate removed:______________________ \n \n \nNumber of applications in response to this notice:_______________ \n \n \n      \nJeanine Boddie-LaVan, Chief Human Resources Officer \nHuman Resources & Employee Development \nValdosta State University \n \nTHIS JOB NOTICE IS POSTED IN CONNECTION WITH THE FILING OF AN \nAPPLICATION FOR PERMANENT ALIEN LABOR CERTIFICATION FOR THE ABOVE \nJOB OPPORTUNITY. ANY PERSON MAY PROVIDE DOCUMENTARY EVIDENCE \nBEARING ON THE APPLICATION TO THE CERTIFYING OFFICER, U.S. DEPARTMENT \nOF LABOR, EMPLOYMENT AND TRAINING ADMINISTRATION, OFFICE OF FOREIGN \nLABOR CERTIFICATION, 200 CONSTITUTION AVENUE NW, ROOM N-5311, \nWASHINGTON, DC 20210. "
    },
